## 3. Micro-Architectural Evidence: Head-of-Line Blocking vs. Cadence Isolation

> **Why this section is here:**  
> High-level latency percentiles don't explain *why* hardware stalls. This section uses NVIDIA Nsight Systems timeline captures to expose the silicon-level conflict: compute-intensive prefill GEMMs monopolizing streaming multiprocessors and evicting the autoregressive decode loop.

### 1. The Collocated Failure Mode: Head-of-Line Blocking

In Collocated serving, when an 8,000-token prompt arrives, the GPU must execute dense matrix multiplications (GEMMs) across all attention and MLP layers. These compute-bound kernels monopolize 100% of the GPU's Streaming Multiprocessors (SMs), forcing in-flight decode iterations to pause.

![Collocated Head-of-Line Blocking](screenshots/trace1_collocated_1xtp2.png)

> **Trace 1 Micro-Evidence (`trace1_collocated_1x_tp2_burst.nsys-rep`):**
> * **Silicon Observation:** During prompt injection (24.65s – 25.46s), compute-heavy prefill GEMMs (`ampere_bf16_s16816gemm`) saturate all 108 SMs on both GPUs.
> * **Head-of-Line Blocking:** Autoregressive decode iteration on Stream 17 is completely halted for **810 ms**, directly causing a 274 ms P99 ITL spike for active concurrent users.
> * **Driver Overhead:** GPU execution time is 63.7% dominated by prefill GEMMs, leaving decode attention starved down to only 6.8% of compute cycles.

---

### 2. The Disaggregated Defense: Cadence Isolation

In Disaggregated serving, incoming prompts are routed to dedicated prefill GPUs. The decode GPU's execution queue is completely insulated from prefill interference.

![Disaggregated Dedicated Decoder Cadence](screenshots/trace2_disagg_decoder.png)

> **Trace 2 Micro-Evidence (`trace2_disagg_1p1d_burst.nsys-rep`):**
> * **Silicon Observation:** Orange CUDA Graph executions on Stream 7 run continuously at a steady **~14 ms cadence** (75.2% of kernel runtime in `ampere_bf16_s16816gemm_64x64_sliced`).
> * **Zero Prefill Interference:** The decoder experiences **0.0% prefill GEMMs**—new prompt arrivals do not induce any SM warp contention.
> * **Batch Transition Tax:** At the transition boundary (+250ms to +265ms), vLLM swaps CUDA Graph handles (`Graph 11428` to `Graph 11425`) and ingests remote KV blocks in just **~15 ms**, immediately resuming autoregressive generation.

---

### 3. Tensor Parallelism Barrier Tax (TP=2 vs. Independent TP=1 Replicas)

When sharding model weights across GPUs using Tensor Parallelism (TP=2), every single autoregressive decode step forces both GPUs into lock-step synchronization:

![TP=2 NCCL Barriers](screenshots/trace5_tp2_nccl_barriers.png)

> **Trace 5 Micro-Evidence (`trace5_collocated_2x_tp2_allreduce.nsys-rep`):**
> * **Lock-Step Synchronization:** GPU 0 (`Worker_TP0`) and GPU 1 (`Worker_TP1`) must synchronize intermediate activation vectors after every self-attention and MLP layer.
> * **The NCCL Kernel Tax:** Profile reports (`trace5_cuda_gpu_kern_sum.csv`) show **3.2% of total GPU kernel time spent executing `ncclDevKernel_AllGather_RING_LL`** (2,050 calls, 16.9 µs average per call).
> * **The TP=1 Alternative (Trace 6):** Serving 2 independent TP=1 replicas eliminates inter-GPU communication entirely (**0.0% NCCL overhead**), giving each GPU 100% compute/memory bandwidth for independent request streams.

---

### 4. Asymmetric Disaggregation & Chunked Prefill (1P:3D Architecture)

In long-context serving, prefill is compute-bound and transient, while decode is memory-bandwidth-bound and persistent. Asymmetric disaggregation (1 Prefill : 3 Decode) balances cluster resource utilization:

![Asymmetric 1P:3D Prefill Burst](screenshots/trace8_1p3d_asymmetric_prefill.png)

> **Trace 8 Micro-Evidence (`trace8_disagg_1p3d_asymmetric.nsys-rep`):**
> * **Chunked Prefill Execution:** The dedicated prefill instance on GPU 0 processes long prompts in 2,048-token chunked passes (`execute_context_2(2048)`), saturating Tensor Cores for ~200 ms without blowing up activation memory.
> * **Asynchronous KV Cache Dispatch:** On Stream 3952, KV cache blocks are dispatched asynchronously across the interconnect to 3 downstream decode instances, immediately freeing the prefiller to accept the next prompt while decoders generate tokens in parallel.

