### The Saturation Boundary Takeaway:
* At open-loop rates below saturation ($\lambda \le 4.3\text{ req/s}$), requests arrive spaced $\ge 230\text{ ms}$ apart. Collocated vLLM's chunked prefill (512-token chunks) easily interleaves prompt chunks between decode iterations, keeping P99 ITL at $\le 20\text{ ms}$. 
* **Conclusion:** Deploying Disaggregation under light-to-medium traffic is an **expensive anti-pattern**—it degrades TTFT by $2\times$ to $3\times$ while providing negligible ITL benefit.

