## 6. Hardware Interconnect Tax: NVLink vs. 100G InfiniBand

> **Why this section is here:**  
> Disaggregation requires moving KV-cache tensors across physical buses. This section quantifies the physical wire cost of transferring an 8,192-token KV cache ($1.15\text{ GB}$) across **600 GB/s NVLink** vs. **100 Gbps InfiniBand RDMA**, demonstrating the "Interconnect Decoupling Invariant".

### Network Micro-Benchmarking: 8k Context Transfer Cost

| Metric | Intra-Node NVLink 12 (`disagg_1p1d`) | 100G InfiniBand RDMA (`disagg_1p1d_ib`) | Impact Factor |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Raw Bus Bandwidth** | **600.0 GB/s** (bidirectional) | **12.5 GB/s** (100 Gbps raw) | $48\times$ raw bandwidth disparity |
| **Effective KV Transfer Speed** | **20.24 GB/s** | **1.14 GB/s** | $17.8\times$ effective transfer delta |
| **Transfer Stream GPU Time** | **Stream 3952:** **$1.1\%$** | **Stream 4004:** **$29.4\%$** | **$27\times$ longer stream occupancy** |
| **CUDA Driver Sync Stalls** | 64 calls ($0.6\text{ s}$ total) | **293,328 calls ($2.02\text{ s}$, 48.5% driver time)** | **$4,500\times$ more driver synchronization** |
| **Memory Copy Driver Time** | 340 calls ($3.5\text{ ms}$) | **293,328 calls ($1.04\text{ s}$, 25.0% driver time)** | **$300\times$ more driver memcpy overhead** |
| **Aggregate Driver Stalls** | $<1.0\%$ of runtime | **73.5% of total CUDA API time** | Host CPU thread completely stalled |
| **Added TTFT Latency (8k prompt)** | **+59.7 ms** | **+927.7 ms** | **$+0.93\text{ s}$ network penalty per request** |
| **P99 ITL (Decode Cadence)** | **14.8 ms** | **15.1 ms** | **0.0% impact on token generation** |

---

#### Visualizing the Interconnect Tax in Nsight: NVLink vs. 100G InfiniBand

#### 1. Cross-Node 100G InfiniBand: Network Staging & Serialization Stalls
Transferring an 8,192-token KV cache ($1.15\text{ GB}$) across a 100 Gbps network link forces the GPU compute engine into an idle bubble while chunked Host-to-Device (HtoD) memory copies saturate the interconnect stream:

![100G InfiniBand KV Transfer Stall](screenshots/trace4_infiniband_transfer_stall.png)

> **Trace 4 Micro-Evidence (`trace4_disagg_2p2d_infiniband_8k.nsys-rep`):**
> * **The ~1-Second Network Bubble:** Under Stream 4004, `100.0% HtoD memcpy` runs for **951.77 ms** (`execute_context_0(0)_generation_0(0)`).
> * **Compute Starvation:** Stream 17 sits completely empty—the decoder cannot launch a single CUDA Graph forward pass until all remote KV cache blocks have traversed the NIC and PCIe bus.
> * **Driver Tax:** Profile reports show **293,328 calls to `cuStreamSynchronize` (2,016 ms wait)** and **293,328 calls to `cuMemcpyAsync` (1,040 ms)**, causing 73.5% of total CUDA API time to be lost in driver spin-waits.

#### 2. Intra-Node NVLink: Sub-Millisecond Peer-to-Peer Transfer
When running within a single server chassis across NVLink ($150\text{ GB/s}$ unidirectional / $600\text{ GB/s}$ aggregate), KV-cache blocks are ingested directly via Peer-to-Peer zero-copy memory handles:

![NVLink Peer-to-Peer KV Transfer](screenshots/trace3_nvlink_p2p_transfer.png)

> **Trace 3 Micro-Evidence (`trace3_disagg_1p1d_nvlink_8k.nsys-rep`):**
> * **Zero-Copy IPC:** NVLink leverages `cuIpcOpenMemHandle_v2` (5.78 ms), mapping remote GPU buffers directly into the decoder's virtual address space.
> * **Immediate Compute Handoff:** Stream 3952 completes `100.0% PtoP memcpy` with a microscopic 18.11 ms context ingestion pass (`execute_context_1`), after which the engine immediately locks into continuous **~14 ms CUDA Graph decode steps**.

### The Interconnect Decoupling Invariant:
A critical systems takeaway: **Interconnect bandwidth heavily taxes TTFT, but has ZERO impact on ITL.** Once the KV cache arrives in the decoder's local HBM, autoregressive generation runs exclusively against local high-bandwidth memory at $\sim 15\text{ ms/tok}$.

