## 8. Production Decision Matrix: When to Disaggregate

> **Why this section is here:**  
> Provides an actionable heuristic decision tree for ML infrastructure teams evaluating whether to adopt P/D disaggregation.

```
                              Incoming Serving Workload
                                          │
                   ┌──────────────────────┴──────────────────────┐
                   ▼                                             ▼
          Short/Medium Prompts                          Long-Context / RAG
        (Chat / Code Gen, ≤2k in)                       (Enterprise RAG, ≥8k in)
                   │                                             │
                   ▼                                             ▼
       STAY COLLOCATED (TP=1 or TP=2)                 What is your traffic pattern?
       • Zero KV serialization tax                               │
       • 100% dynamic GPU pooling                 ┌──────────────┴──────────────┐
       • Up to 25% higher throughput              ▼                             ▼
                                        Light/Medium Poisson           Heavy Concurrency ($C \ge 4$)
                                         ($\lambda \le 4\text{ req/s}$)    or Sudden Burst Spikes
                                                  │                             │
                                                  ▼                             ▼
                                           STAY COLLOCATED              DEPLOY DISAGGREGATION
                                           • Chunked prefill handles    • Protects P99 ITL (<20 ms)
                                             prompt load with no stall  • Isolates active streams
                                           • 2x-3x faster TTFT          • Requires NVLink / high-BW fabric
```

