## 9. Reproduction Guide & Benchmark Suite

> **Why this section is here:**  
> Step-by-step instructions to run the benchmarking suite and extract the Nsight profiling traces.

### 1. Launching Collocated Serving (2x TP1 Baseline)
```bash
# Terminal 1: Launch Collocated Instance A (GPU 0)
CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0 vllm serve Qwen/Qwen3-8B --port 8001 --gpu-memory-utilization 0.90

# Terminal 2: Launch Collocated Instance B (GPU 1)
CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=1 vllm serve Qwen/Qwen3-8B --port 8002 --gpu-memory-utilization 0.90
```

### 2. Launching Disaggregated Serving (1P:1D via NIXL)
```bash
# Terminal 1: Launch Prefill Instance (GPU 0)
CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0 vllm serve Qwen/Qwen3-8B --port 8100 --gpu-memory-utilization 0.90 \
  --kv-transfer-config '{"kv_connector":"NixlConnector","kv_role":"kv_producer","kv_rank":0,"kv_parallel_size":2}'

# Terminal 2: Launch Decode Instance (GPU 1)
CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=1 vllm serve Qwen/Qwen3-8B --port 8200 --gpu-memory-utilization 0.90 \
  --kv-transfer-config '{"kv_connector":"NixlConnector","kv_role":"kv_consumer","kv_rank":1,"kv_parallel_size":2}'
```

### 3. Profiling with NVIDIA Nsight Systems
```bash
# Capture full kernel and driver timeline during an 8k burst
nsys profile \
  --trace=cuda,nvtx,osrt \
  --cuda-memory-usage=true \
  --output=results/traces/trace_custom \
  --force-overwrite=true \
  vllm serve Qwen/Qwen3-8B --port 8000 ...
```
